    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 94365 'Robgoblin Pondblasters!' (title), 95048 (card), objective 103235; icon 11209."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter: reference Npcs.json Id 4499 drawn at [-1038.8, -55.87, 1089.62] (npc_spawns_extra.json spawn_guid 100000004499, FreeRealms-Legacy FabledRealms.lua). Region The Wilds, place Stillwater Crossing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 84 ('Robgoblin Pondblasters! (the live random encounter: robgoblins fishing with dynamite)'): scene sg_random_encounter_creek, entry, exit, 3 waves, 10 spawns ({'Robgoblin Pondblaster': 9, 'Robgoblin Boomer': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1243 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_creek has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Robgoblin Pondblasters!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Frostfang Snarlers!' (Warrior’s Cudgel of Cleaving; Wizard's Sparkle Twig of Glaciers; Medic's Reflex Hammer of Vitals; Brawler's Mallet of Rumbling), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Frostfang Snarlers!' (revision 48736), one per combat job, and 2 coins. The same pages also name Bixie Hive, Cracked Claw Caverns, Hot Springs Haven, Sheep Watch. Brawler: the wiki's 'Bell Brawler Gloves' is 'Saved by the Bell Brawler Gloves' in our record dungeons/frostfang_snarlers.json."
    }
  ]
